There are two conversions we need to do: kilometers to meters, and hours to minutes. Let's look at kilometers to meters.

Since $1\,\text{kilometer}=1000\,\text{meters}$, we know that both $\dfrac{1\,\text{kilometer}}{1000\,\text{meters}}$ and $\dfrac{1000\,\text{meters}}{1\,\text{kilometer}}$ equal $1$.

So we can multiply by either of those fractions to help us convert units, since multiplying by $1$ doesn't change value. In this problem, we multiply by $\blueD{\dfrac{1000\,\text{meters}}{1\,\text{kilometer}}}$ since the rate we want to convert uses $\text{kilometers}$:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}7\,\dfrac{\cancel{\text{kilometers}}}{\text{hour}}\cdot \blueD{\dfrac{1000\,\text{meters}}{1\,\cancel{\text{kilometer}}}}
\\\\
&=7000\,\dfrac{\text{meters}}{\text{hour}}
\end{align}$
